rebuilt_ROMs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# derived: the reachability walk result, keyed to a fingerprint of the .s files.
# Regenerate with `python3 notes/reachability.py`; never commit it, because a
# stale copy would answer a question about a tree that no longer exists.
notes/.reachability-cache.json

# derived: an image's primary with every .include expanded, for probes whose scan
# is `open(SRC)`.  Regenerate with asm_source.image_path(); never commit one --
# the sources are the source, and a stale expansion would answer for a tree that
# no longer exists.  (notes/.prom_c-image.s was the prom_c-only shim's spelling;
# kept so an older checkout does not start tracking it.)
notes/.image-*.s
notes/.prom_c-image.s

# derived: the DECODE index -- what unidasm says each address decodes to. Keyed
# on the ROM, the unidasm binary and the window parameters, so it is valid until
# one of those changes, and it is what makes a cache-missing run take seconds
# instead of 17 minutes. Regenerated automatically; never commit it.
notes/.reachability-decode.txt
